Package: @PACKAGE@
Name: @NAME@
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: iphoneos-arm
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Author: @AUTHOR@
Section: Fonts
Priority: optional
Depends: firmware (>= 6.0)
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: @HOMEPAGE@
Description: Unicode @EMOJI_VERSION@ colour emoji for iOS 6
 Replaces the stock Apple Color Emoji font with an sbix font built from
 Twemoji @TWEMOJI_VERSION@ artwork covering Unicode Emoji @EMOJI_VERSION@:
 @GLYPH_COUNT@ distinct emoji images, including skin tones, ZWJ professions,
 family sequences, keycaps and regional-indicator flags. Bitmap strikes at
 20, 40, 48 and 96 ppem, so large emoji are sharp instead of upscaled.
 .
 Font metrics are byte-identical to the stock font, so line heights and
 layout do not shift anywhere in the system.
 .
 The stock font is backed up on first install and put back when this
 package is removed. Installing needs about @REQUIRED_MB@ MB free on the
 system partition; the install refuses to start if there is not enough.
 .
 Known limitation: the England, Scotland and Wales tag flags fall back to
 the black flag. iOS 6 CoreText deletes Unicode tag characters before the
 font is consulted, so no font can distinguish those three sequences.
 .
 Artwork is Twemoji, CC-BY 4.0; see /var/lib/@PKGDIRNAME@/COPYING.
